WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.140
Every fall, many monarch butterflies fly south through Virginia.

2
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.720
Every spring, cherry trees in Washington, D.C.

3
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.980
burst into bloom. A butterfly has no calendar.

4
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.220
A tree has no eyes.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.580
So how do plants and animals know when to sleep, bloom, or fly south?

6
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:28.193
Start with one day.

7
00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:33.893
A circadian rhythm is a pattern that repeats about every 24 hours.

8
00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:37.873
Light and darkness help keep it in step with the day.

9
00:00:38.973 --> 00:00:41.813
Many owls hunt at night and rest in the day.

10
00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:44.053
Tree squirrels do the opposite.

11
00:00:45.233 --> 00:00:49.473
In many animals, the rhythm keeps going for a while in steady darkness.

12
00:00:50.173 --> 00:00:53.153
So part of the timing comes from inside the body.

13
00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:57.673
Plants respond too, but they respond by growing.

14
00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:02.133
A tropism is plant growth toward or away from something.

15
00:01:03.173 --> 00:01:04.573
Light shines from one side.

16
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:09.433
Cells on the shaded side of the stem grow longer than cells on the lit side.

17
00:01:10.273 --> 00:01:13.753
The longer side pushes the stem into a bend toward the light.

18
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.023
Now think about a Virginia winter.

19
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:22.263
Days are short, nights are cold, and many foods are hard to find.

20
00:01:23.443 --> 00:01:26.563
Cues like day length and temperature start the responses.

21
00:01:27.843 --> 00:01:29.583
Monarchs migrate south in fall.

22
00:01:30.903 --> 00:01:35.423
Migration is the seasonal movement of animals from one region to another and back.

23
00:01:36.743 --> 00:01:38.423
Dormancy is a resting state.

24
00:01:39.263 --> 00:01:42.583
Growth slows or stops, but the living thing stays alive.

25
00:01:43.483 --> 00:01:45.943
Hibernation is dormancy in animals.

26
00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:50.643
A groundhog's body temperature drops, so it uses less stored fat.

27
00:01:51.417 --> 00:01:53.257
Are these behaviors learned?

28
00:01:54.277 --> 00:02:00.337
Mostly not. An instinct is a behavior an animal inherits and can do without being

29
00:02:00.337 --> 00:02:04.877
taught. A monarch flying south has never made the trip before.

30
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:07.370
So how do they know?

31
00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:12.750
They respond to cues, such as light, day length, and temperature.

32
00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.490
Many of these responses are inherited instincts.

33
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:21.030
Some changes last for many years, like a warming climate.

34
00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.490
Those can shift when these responses happen.
